.Dd October 13, 2026
.Dt FIDOKEYCTL 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm fidokeyctl
.Nd inspect and manage FIDO authenticators
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl d
.Fl i
.Op Fl f Ar device
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
utility inspects and manages FIDO authenticators using
.Xr libfido2 3 .
.Pp
The options are as follows:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl d
Enable libfido2 debugging output.
.It Fl f Ar device
Use the specified FIDO device.
If this option is omitted,
.Nm
automatically selects the device when exactly one authenticator is
available.
.It Fl i
Display information about the authenticator.
.El
.Pp
If more than one FIDO authenticator is present and
.Fl f
is not specified,
.Nm
lists the available devices and exits without selecting one.
.Sh SECURITY
.Nm
uses
.Xr pledge 2
to restrict available system calls.
After device discovery,
.Xr unveil 2
restricts filesystem access to the selected FIDO device.
Once the device has been opened, filesystem access is removed from the
pledged capabilities.
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
.Sh EXAMPLES
Display information about the only connected authenticator:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ fidokeyctl -i
.Ed
.Pp
Select a specific authenticator:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ fidokeyctl -i -f /dev/fido/0
.Ed
.Pp
Enable libfido2 diagnostic output:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ fidokeyctl -d -i
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr ssh-keygen 1 ,
.Xr pledge 2 ,
.Xr unveil 2 ,
.Xr fido 4 ,
.Xr fido_cbor_info_new 3 ,
.Xr fido_dev_info_manifest 3 ,
.Xr fido_dev_open 3
.Sh AUTHORS
.An rboug
